---
title: Thai chicken fried rice
servings: 2
tags: [chicken, stir-fry, quick]
cuisine: thai
source: Thai Chicken Fried Rice by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/chicken-kale-fried-rice
---

Toss the @chicken{150%g} with @seasoning sauce{1%tsp}(Thai, soy-based) and @sugar{1%tsp}.

Heat a #wok{} over medium-high heat. Brown the chicken on one side, then toss until cooked. Set it aside.

Add a little @vegetable oil{} to the wok. Fry the @onion{1/4}(small, diced), @garlic{3-4%cloves}(chopped) and @chili flakes{} to taste until the onion is translucent. Add the @kale stems{2}(thinly sliced on the bias) and stir ~{1%minute}.

Add the @eggs{2}, break the yolks, let them half set, then scramble briefly.

Add the @jasmine rice{350%g}(cooked) and break up any lumps.

Add @soy sauce{2%tsp}, @fish sauce{2%tsp}, @black soy sauce{1/2-1%tsp} and @sugar{1 1/2%tsp}. Toss until every grain is coated and separate. More black soy sauce gives a darker colour.

Add the @kale leaves{2}(cut into ribbons) and @ground white pepper{1/4%tsp} and toss until the kale wilts. Return the chicken and its juices and toss until the rice absorbs them.

Serve at once with a @lime wedge{} and @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped) on top.
